Hi Francesco,

It seems as though your data are currently in "wide" format, but Amelia
usually takes data in "long" format (where each row is a unit-year, as
opposed to each row being one unit). In the wide format, Amelia will
actually use 37 and 39 to impute 38, since each of those is a variable in
the dataset. If you convert to long format, you will have to set the "ts"
and "cs" arguments in order to include the time-series information.

You can see some information on how to reshape your data in the following
question from Stack Exchange:

http://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/7439/how-to-change-data-between-wide-and-long-formats-in-r

Hope that helps!

Cheers,
matt.

